body:
This test only asserts that the `/apps/:appName/system/profile` route renders (with `ProfilePage` mocked), but it doesn’t cover the new behavior introduced in the PR: clicking the Sidebar user-menu “Settings” item should navigate to that route. Add an interaction-based assertion (open user dropdown → click Settings → expect profile page/URL) so the wiring in `AppSidebar` is actually exercised.
```suggestion
    });

    it('navigates to profile page when Settings is clicked in user menu', async () => {
        renderApp();

        // Wait for the app to initialize (sidebar/header shows app label)
        await waitFor(() => {
            const appLabels = screen.getAllByText('Sales App');
            expect(appLabels.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);
        }, { timeout: 10000 });

        // Open the user dropdown in the sidebar.
        // Prefer a button explicitly labeled as the user menu if available.
        const buttons = screen.getAllByRole('button');
        const userMenuButton =
            (buttons.find((btn) => btn.getAttribute('aria-label') === 'User menu')) ??
            buttons[buttons.length - 1];

        fireEvent.click(userMenuButton);

        // Click the "Settings" item in the user menu to navigate to the profile page.
        const settingsItem = await screen.findByText('Settings');
        fireEvent.click(settingsItem);

        // Expect the profile page to be rendered after navigation.
        await waitFor(() => {
            expect(screen.getByTestId('profile-page')).toBeInTheDocument();
        }, { timeout: 10000 });
    });
```
